From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:27:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iio: adc: allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc: Add the
 A733 compatible

The A733 GPADC has seven 12-bit channels for 0 to 1.8 V (A733 manual,
18.12.1) and the same register layout as the D1 GPADC at every offset
the sun20i-gpadc driver uses (18.12.8). Add
"allwinner,sun60i-a733-gpadc" with "allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc" as the
fallback, so the existing driver binds without a change.

Unlike the D1, the A733 has a bus gate and a separate 24 MHz module
clock (4.1.6.170, 4.1.6.171), so it takes the two clocks "bus" and
"mod" like the A523 and the schema requires both.

Not covered: the reference select (GP_RVLT_SEL) and the sampling-time
registers, which the driver does not use.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the driver binds through the fallback and
converts the wired channels to the voltages of the board dividers.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/iio/adc/allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc.yaml        | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc.yaml
index 6467800d30e2..9393aa203655 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - enum:
               - allwinner,sun50i-h616-gpadc
+              - allwinner,sun60i-a733-gpadc
           - const: allwinner,sun20i-d1-gpadc
 
   "#io-channel-cells":
@@ -50,8 +51,10 @@ allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
-          enum:
-            - allwinner,sun55i-a523-gpadc
+          contains:
+            enum:
+              - allwinner,sun55i-a523-gpadc
+              - allwinner,sun60i-a733-gpadc
     then:
       properties:
         clocks:
